cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ggc-kinetics, please cite it as below."
title: "ggc-kinetics: exact enzyme progress-curve solvers, detection statistics and a plate-reader parser"
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24409789
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/bpmcginley/ggc-kinetics"
authors:
  - family-names: "McGinley"
    given-names: "Bruce"
    affiliation: "University of Massachusetts Amherst"
keywords:
  - enzyme kinetics
  - progress curves
  - Michaelis-Menten
  - Lambert W
  - plate reader
abstract: >-
  Closed-form and split-step solvers for enzyme progress curves (product inhibition, enzyme decay, coupled lag,
  slow binding, tight binding, substrate inhibition), two detection statistics, and a parser for plate-reader
  text exports. Detector thresholds are ASSUMED values calibrated on MODELED (simulated) plates only.
